<title>UK: UK unemployment falls 68,200 in Feb.</title>
<headline>UK unemployment falls 68,200 in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released the following provisional data for UK unemployment in February. (Previous estimates for January in brackets, data seasonally adjusted unless indicated)</p>
<p>    UNEMPLOYMENT		    FEB	 JAN     (PREL JAN)</p>
<p>    Monthly change		-68,200   -68,600   (-67,800)</p>
<p>    Rate (pct)			6.2*	6.5	   (6.5)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj change  -80,000     n/a     (+39,600)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj rate	6.5	 6.8	   (6.8)</p>
<p>NOTE - Consensus forecast was for seasonally adjusted fall of 40,000 in February.  </p>
<p>    Unemployment level (million)   1,746.3    1,814.5    1,815</p>
<p>    Unemployment level unadj   1,827.8    1.907.8    1,908</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 3m	-61,200    -70,200  -70,000</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 6m	-60,400    -51,900  -51,800</p>
<p>   AVERAGE EARNINGS			  JAN	DEC (PREL DEC)</p>
<p>   underlying yearly chng (pct)	  5.0	4.75   (4.25)</p>
<p>   index (base 1990)		     136.3     135.7  (135.2)</p>
<p>   actual yearly chng (pct)		4.9	4.9     (4.5)</p>
<p>By sector (annual pct chng)</p>
<p>   Production-- underlying		 5.0	4.75   (4.75)</p>
<p>		 -- actual		     4.3	5.2     (4.9)</p>
<p>   Manufacturing  -- underlying	  4.75     4.75   (4.75)</p>
<p>			-- actual		4.2	5.0     (4.8)</p>
<p>   Services  -- underlying		 5.0	4.5     (4.0)</p>
<p>		 -- actual		     5.2	4.6     (4.5)</p>
<p>NOTE: consensus forecast 4.25 pct for overall underlying average earnings.</p>
<p>    UNIT WAGE COSTS	    JAN	   DEC   (PREL DEC)</p>
<p>    Monthly change vs yr ago 2.7	   2.8     (2.4)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)	  115.2	115.8  (115.5)</p>
<p>    3-mth versus same yr/ago 3.1	  3.4	(3.2)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)	  115.3	115.1  (114.8)</p>
<p>PRODUCTIVITY</p>
<p>    monthly change vs yr ago 1.5	   2.2    (+2.4)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)	  122.1	 122.0 (122.2)</p>
<p>    3mth vs same year ago    1.4	   1.1    (+1.3)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)	  121.9	 121.8 (122.0)</p>
<p>OVERALL EMPLOYMENT (THOUSANDS, S/ADJ)</p>
<p>    WORKFORCE IN EMPLOYMENT	   Q4	 Q3     Q4 95</p>
<p>    LEVEL				   26,147 26,100 25,925</p>
<p>    CHANGE					47    216    148</p>
<p>    EMPLOYEES IN EMPLOYMENT	   22,363 22,308 22,142</p>
<p>						    54    115    145</p>
<p>    JOB CENTRE VACANCIES		FEB	  JAN</p>
<p>    change				 +7,800     -3,200 (-3,500)</p>
<p>    level				 270,900   263,100</p>
<p>    Avg 3m change			   700	 200    (100)</p>
<p>The ONS said the 6.2 percent unemployment rate in February was the lowest since November 1990 and the lowest level since October 1990.  </p>
<p>Annual average earnings growth of 5.0% is the highest since November 1992.</p>
</text>
